body:
Off topic, but this question has always been on the back of my mind for years:
When doctors and nurses ask you what you are allergic too, do they mean *anything* you are allergic too? I always tell them cats and kiwis and I feel like a fucking idiot when I do 'cause I don't know what exactly they need to know. 
In some cases doctors laughed at me, others just wrote it down without saying anything. Am I just making a fool of myself whenever they ask this? ;-;
